PlantGuard UAV database migrations
==================================

Alembic is the only production schema-management path. Application startup must
not call ``Base.metadata.create_all()``.

The migration environment reads an explicitly injected ``sqlalchemy.url`` first.
This is used by isolated tests and administrative tooling. When no URL is
injected, it loads the validated PlantGuard settings and unwraps the database URL
only when creating the migration engine. The URL is never written to logs.

Common commands, run from the repository root after installing the persistence
dependencies:

    alembic upgrade head
    alembic current
    alembic downgrade -1
    alembic upgrade head --sql

Create future revisions with:

    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the schema change"

Always review generated revisions before applying them. Back up production data
before destructive migrations. The first revision remains an intentionally empty
baseline; later revisions build the application schema from that stable starting
point. The current schema includes the saved-field selection projection and must
continue to evolve only through reviewed Alembic revisions.
